anchor_informal:
Let $X$ and $Y$ be locally ringed spaces, and let $f \colon X \to Y$ be a morphism between them. For any open set $U \subseteq Y$ and a point $x \in X$ such that $f(x) \in U$, the following diagram commutes:
\[
\begin{CD}
\mathcal{O}_Y(U) @>{\text{germ}_{f(x)}}>> (\mathcal{O}_Y)_{f(x)} \\
@V{f^\#_U}VV @VV{f_{\text{stalk},x}}V \\
\mathcal{O}_X(f^{-1}(U)) @>{\text{germ}_x}>> (\mathcal{O}_X)_x
\end{CD}
\]
where $\mathcal{O}_X$ and $\mathcal{O}_Y$ are the structure sheaves of $X$ and $Y$ respectively, $\text{germ}$ denotes the germ maps, and $f_{\text{stalk},x}$ is the stalk map induced by $f$ at $x$.

